Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:43:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(wallet-link): replace %ROWTYPE with jsonb to fix
 Supabase compilation error
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ERROR ON SUPABASE
----------------
When applying the migration on Supabase, this error appeared:

  ERROR: 42P01: relation "public.get_verified_reward_identity"
          does not exist
  CONTEXT: compilation of PL/pgSQL function
           "get_wallet_reward_balance" near line 4

ROOT CAUSE
----------
The migration declared PL/pgSQL variables as:

  v_identity public.get_verified_reward_identity%ROWTYPE;

%ROWTYPE only works for tables/views/typed relations, NOT for
functions returning scalar/composite types like jsonb. PL/pgSQL
tried to resolve public.get_verified_reward_identity as a relation
during function compilation (it isn't — it's a function), so the
lookup failed with 42P01.

THE FIX
-------
Change the variable type from
  public.get_verified_reward_identity%ROWTYPE
to
  jsonb
and access fields with the ->> / -> operators:

  v_identity := public.get_verified_reward_identity(p_wallet_address);
  v_solana_wallet := v_identity->>'solana_wallet';
  -- linked_evm_wallets is a jsonb array; convert to text[]:
  select array_agg(elem::text) into v_linked_evm_wallets_arr
    from jsonb_array_elements_text(
      coalesce(v_identity->'linked_evm_wallets', '[]'::jsonb)
    ) AS elem;

VERIFICATION
------------
- All 58 Node static tests pass.
- All 35 Python migration static tests pass (added a new
  test_get_wallet_reward_balance_resolves_verified_identity test).
- All 6 Python accounting scenario tests pass (S1-S5 + cross-identity
  hijack).
- The migration parses cleanly with pglast (real Postgres parser):
    43 top-level statements parsed (3 CREATE TABLE, 6 CREATE FUNCTION,
    18 GRANT, 12 CREATE INDEX, 3 ALTER TABLE, 1 INSERT).
- New script: scripts/validate_migration_parses.py — re-run anytime
  to verify the SQL parses before applying to Supabase.

AFFECTED FUNCTIONS
------------------
- public.get_wallet_reward_balance(text) — variable v_identity now jsonb
- public.claim_reward(text, text, numeric, text, jsonb) — variable
  v_identity now jsonb

No data changes. No structural changes. The fix is purely in the
PL/pgSQL variable declaration syntax — it does NOT affect the
accounting model (still per-wallet consumption via
wallet_point_consumption + FIFO distribution + MIGRATION_BACKFILL
preservation).
